A||N||42||Monkeyman||THE MONKEYMAN RETURNETH||||1||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||02-14-2000||09:01 AM||||Disclaimer--This post is liable to get long-winded so, if you don't care who I am or what I'm about, don't waste your time reading this.<P>As many of you who are active in this forum have noticed, I've detached myself from this group lately.  I would like to explain some of the reasons why.  I have always been the "class clown" (not my words, but they seem to fit quite well) and I have enjoyed the job.  I'm not a very technical person and this was the way I've always fit in.  I enjoy making others laugh although my dry sense of humor is difficult to understand at times.  There are some here that do not appreciate my humor for what ever reason.  I remember on thread where I posted 3 or 4 times in a row.  (This had to do with "Standing By").  Sometimes it takes more than one post to make a joke.  Through my humor, I have pissed some members off. This was not intentional and I offer no apologies.  I haven't meant to anger anyone, so I feel that I've done nothing wrong.<BR>There have been some remarks posted here that have been less than positive towards me.  Everyone is entitled to their own opinion, but I believe some of them have gotten slightly out of hand.  A comment was made that I was a sensitive guy.  This is true (call it one of my character defects).  If you know that someone is overly sensitive (right or wrong) it would make sense to be a little gentler with your words towards him/her.  If this was the only slight, I could have/should have/would have gotten over it.  Unfortunately, this did not stop there.  During the past 2 weeks, I have received 7 very nasty, rude and abusive emails.  One "gentleman" (I use this term very loosely) was even creative enough to scan and attach a picture of his middle finger.  This is totally uncalled for.  I felt that my "services" were unwanted.  I had no intention of remaining a part of a community that didn't want me around.  It has been said numerous times here and privately, "If you don't have anything nice to say, don't say anything at all!".  I wish to be an active, well-liked member of PFF, but I will not tolerate any abuse!  It has been suggested (by more than one member [privately] thanx for the support) that I should name names so that some ass-whooping could commence.  I refused to reveal the names of those who were so rude to me.  I think that, for the most part, email is a private thing and should stay that way.  I also didn't want to start any flame wars.  I truly love this forum and I don't want to be a part of anything that will hurt, maim, or destroy it.  I will remain an active part of this forum irregardless of what others desire.  If Cliff ever decides to erase my name from the roster, he may do so (it's his forum), but I will not give any of you the power to do so again.  I want to thank those of you who have chosen to remain my friend through this.  These are true friends.  There are those I choose to like and those I choose to simply tolerate, but I will treat everyone with the same respect I always have.  I expect the same in return.  This was once a "family" and I hope it will be again. <BR>I wish to address one thread and then I'll leave this alone for good.  In regards to the "God" thread in O/T, I feel very strongly about my beliefs.  As a matter of fact, I feel stronger about this than anything else.  If anyone took my posts as personally offensive and wishes to discuss this, feel free to email me privately.  If you choose to speak privately, be adult.  As I said before, I will not tolerate the kind of abusive email I have recently received.  <BR>I'm not very eloquent (I've been up all night-just be happy I can still remember how to turn the computer on!).  This thread has been slightly disjointed and I've certainly rambled on.  I look forward to any comments regarding this (either privately or on the forum), but remember, "<B>IF YOU CAN'T SAY ANYTHING NICE, DON'T SAY ANYTHING AT ALL!!!</B><P>Cheers!<BR>Dave "Monkeyman" Gray   <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||02-14-2000||09:25 AM||||Welcome back, Monkey!  Somehow I missed out on the fact that there were harsh words exchanged (probably because I didn't read the God thread).  All I knew is I was missing Monkeyman's jokes.<P>There ought to be room on this forum for anybody who likes Fieros, regardless of their other beliefs.  There simply aren't enough of us Fiero nuts for us to get fragmented (notch v. fastback, 6 cyl vs. 4 cyl, etc).  The only way we get any respect is to stand together.<P>We don't want to end up like Speedvision's motorsports message boards.  They started out as a rational discussion of motorsports and quickly devolved into a bunch of dip$hits insulting one another's racial heritage, sexual orientation, etc - crap like "You like Jeff Gordon.  You must be a fag."||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||02-14-2000||09:29 AM||||Monkey, I want to be among the first to welcome you back!  While we haven't chatted often, I do appreciate your form of disjointed humor!  <P>Opinions, it has been said, are best kept to oneself... of course, opinions are also what makes us who we are.  Thruogh my own experieces, I have learned not to tread where I shouldn't... for that reason, I stayed away from the religion topic.  While I do enjoy many of the off topic post, I see where it can lead. <P>Most of all, I appreciate what Cliff has done, in bringing Fiero owners from around the world together... so much so, that one day, I would like to have the opportunity to meet some of you, as I am probably the only member in North Carolina this will be difficult.  <P>Anyway, enough of my own sappy rambling.<P>WELCOME BACK MONKEY!!!!!!!!<P>Brian Hooper<BR>Greensboro, NC||||reg||1
Z||000003||BOILERMAKER||02-14-2000||09:54 AM||||Wow, a lot has happened in the past couple of weeks and I didn't even realize it.  I guess I will have to pay more attention.  Sorry to hear that you have been treated in such an abrassive manner.  <P>Hmmm, just keep in mind that what goes around comes around Monkeyman.  Welcome back.  I would hate for someone such as you leave because of childish remarks from other people (membors or non-members).||||reg||1
Z||000004||BOILERMAKER||02-14-2000||10:28 AM||||Just got done reading the Post that might have started this whole thing and ... well, WOW!<P>Anyway, the truth is like a double-edged sword and I guess the truth really got to a few people.  Just remember, Monkey, that those who weather the trials and tribulations here on earth for the sake of Christianity will be rewarded so much more up in Heaven.||||reg||1
